# EMIT: a table of literals bound INSIDE a function body.
#
# THIS IS A SILENT-WRONG-ANSWER FIXTURE, not a crash fixture. A full-native
# function that bound a table codegen could not type emitted `void* t = NULL`
# and DISCARDED THE INITIALIZER — no diagnostic, no warning — so every element
# read back as NULL. Where the elements were strings the NULL reached
# `strlen` and the program died with SIGSEGV 139 (`examples/boring/roman.id`);
# where they were numbers it would simply have answered wrongly. The
# module-scope form of the same table had been lowered natively for some time,
# so the defect was one scope wide and nothing looked at that scope.
#
# All three element kinds are here because the classification is per-kind, and
# a lowering that handles only the kind whose failure happened to segfault
# would leave the quiet half in place. Index 2 in each, so a table that lost
# its tail and a table that lost its head both fail.
# expect: CM 900 2.5
# @corpus current
pick: str = (i: i64)
  glyph = { "M", "CM", "D" }
  glyph(i)

num: i64 = (i: i64)
  value = { 1000, 900, 500 }
  value(i)

frac: f64 = (i: i64)
  parts = { 1.5, 2.5, 3.5 }
  parts(i)

a = pick(2)
b = num(2)
c = frac(2)
print("{a} {b} {c}")
